# Learnings

Append dated notes. Promote durable rules to `.cursor/rules/` / `docs/*/decisions.md`.

## 2026-08-14

- Activity UI bug: opening a category `<select>` briefly puts the widget window in the OS foreground; the 2s poll (`poll.ts`) then classifies it as `ignored` (Lattice window), and the live `activity-updated` push re-renders `ActivityNowCard`/`ActivityTopLists`, unmounting the `<select>` and closing the native dropdown mid-pick. Fix: `useActivityWidget.setCategoryMenuOpen` freezes `onActivityUpdated`→`setSummary` while any category select has focus, and refetches once on close (guarded against a fast reopen racing that refetch). Chromium often **skips `blur`** when a focused `<select>` becomes `disabled` (`busy` after `correct()`), which used to leave the freeze stuck until app restart — unfreeze on `onChange` + when `disabled` becomes true, and re-freeze on `mousedown` so a still-focused select can be opened again. The three category `<select>`s share `activity/CategorySelect.tsx`.
- Stale "Maintenant" video after closing a YouTube tab: `poll.ts` falls back to the media-bridge's last reported domain/title (`getMediaPlaybackDomain/Title`) when `active-url.exe`/title parsing can't resolve the real current tab. That state only self-heals via `MEDIA_TTL_MS` (was 45s) or an extension `chrome.tabs.onRemoved` — if that event is ever missed (e.g. MV3 service worker restart wiping `tabFrames` mid-flight, or one ad-iframe's `playing:true` never followed by `false`), the stale video can look "current" well beyond one heartbeat. Hardened both sides: `MEDIA_TTL_MS` 45s→20s (`electron/activity/mediaBridge.ts`) and per-frame age filtering `FRAME_STALE_MS`=20s in `extensions/lattice-media/background.js`'s `playingDomains()` (content heartbeats every 8s, so a real still-playing foreground tab never hits this).

## 2026-08-13

- Activity tracking: YouTube is **per video** (title / video id), not one `youtube.com` entertainment bucket — remove domain default + generic title pattern `youtube`. Search engines (`google.com`, bing, ddg…) excluded from active time. System exes collapsed to a single Top apps row « Système ».
- Activity: `ActivityCategory` is no longer a fixed union — it is a `string`. Builtins stay in `BUILTIN_CATEGORIES`; user categories live in `rules.json` as `customCategories: [{ id, label, color }]`. CRUD via IPC `add/update/delete-activity-category`. Deleting remaps rules → `other` and reclassifies today’s JSONL. UI ring + Options manager. Legacy UI snapshot removed (2026-08-13 evening).
- Activity UI aligned to README screenshots: shared `WidgetTitlebar` (settings / hide / close), hero row (total + ring + legend), tinted category pill selects, minimal footer with actions behind ⋯, Pause/AFK switches on Options page.

## 2026-08-10

- Activity: category `studies` (Études); manual AFK toggle (`manualAfk`); default idle threshold 60s; corrections reclassify today’s segments + `buildSummary` applies live rules so UI selects/bars refresh.

## 2026-08-09

- Browser quotas (work/entertainment): classify by **site/video domain**, not the browser process. For `BROWSER_APPS`, domain beats `userAppOverrides` on brave/chrome; Now-card corrections with a domain use scope `domain`; Top apps skips browser+domain (Top sites owns that time); media bridge origin fills domain when UIA/title miss.

